## Architecture

### Packages (`src/{{ project_slug }}/` and `src/agent_work/`)
Project-specific importable code lives in `src/{{ project_slug }}/`; the
serial GitLab issue runner lives in `src/agent_work/`. Do not place importable
production code at the repository top level.

### Tests (`tests/`)
Pytest test suite. Fixtures are in `conftest.py`.

### Configuration (`pyproject.toml`)
Single source of truth for project metadata, dependencies, ruff rules, pytest options, tox environments, and coverage settings.

Python console commands are declared in `[project.scripts]` and delegate into
this installed package.

### Bash applications (`bin/` and `src/` or `lib/`)
When this project adds Bash, expose one user-facing command in `bin/`. Keep
sourceable implementation and library files in a separate `src/` or `lib/`
directory. Tests and clearly labeled development or CI helpers remain outside
production code and are not additional user entry points.

